text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'As long as Thunderstaff is untapped, if a creature would deal combat damage to you, prevent 1 of that damage.\\n{2}, {T}: Attacking creatures get +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Choose one —\\n• Create a 5/5 green Beast creature token.\\n• Create five 1/1 green Insect creature tokens.\\nEntwine {G}{G}{G} (Choose both if you pay the entwine cost.)', 'Coastal Tower enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}.', "Create X 2/2 white Cat creature tokens. Shuffle White Sun's Zenith into its owner's library.", 'Creatures your opponents control get -2/-0 until end of turn.', "Defender (This creature can't attack.)", "Defender\\nMetalcraft — As long as you control three or more artifacts, Spire Serpent gets +2/+2 and can attack as though it didn't have defender.", "Destroy target artifact creature or black creature. It can't be regenerated.", "Destroy target artifact or creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target creature, then proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', 'Draw three cards. Then discard two cards unless you discard an artifact card.', 'Each player puts a creature card from their graveyard onto the battlefield.', 'Each player sacrifices a creature.', 'Each player sacrifices two creatures.', "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block, and its activated abilities can't be activated.", 'Equipped creature gets +0/+6.\\nEquip {3} ({3}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery. This card enters the battlefield unattached and stays on the battlefield if the creature leaves.)', 'Equipped creature gets +1/+0 and has first strike.\\nEquip {1}', 'Equipped creature gets +2/+0.\\nEquip {1}', 'Equipped creature gets +2/+2 and has infect. (It deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nWhenever Grafted Exoskeleton becomes unattached from a permanent, sacrifice that permanent.\\nEquip {2}', "Equipped creature has shroud. (It can't be the target of spells or abilities.)\\n{U}{U}: Attach Neurok Stealthsuit to target creature you control.\\nEquip {1} ({1}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)", "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)\\nWhenever a player casts a spell, sacrifice a creature.", 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nVigilance\\nIndestructible (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy this creature. If its toughness is 0 or less, it\'s still put into its owner\'s graveyard.)', 'Flying', 'Flying\\nIndestructible (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy this creature.)', 'Flying\\nInfect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nSacrifice a creature: Flesh-Eater Imp gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nMetalcraft — {U}: Exile Argent Sphinx. Return it to the battlefield under your control at the beginning of the next end step. Activate only if you control three or more artifacts.', "Flying\\nYou can't lose the game and your opponents can't win the game.", "Forbidding Watchtower enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {W}.\\n{1}{W}: Forbidding Watchtower becomes a 1/5 white Soldier creature until end of turn. It's still a land.", "Imprint — When Duplicant enters the battlefield, you may exile target nontoken creature.\\nAs long as a card exiled with Duplicant is a creature card, Duplicant has the power, toughness, and creature types of the last creature card exiled with Duplicant. It's still a Shapeshifter.", 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nPhyrexian Juggernaut attacks each combat if able.', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nWhen Viridian Corrupter enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact.', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Rot Wolf this turn dies, you may draw a card.', 'Infect (This creature deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)\\n{T}: Add {C}.', 'Living weapon (When this Equipment enters the battlefield, create a 0/0 black Phyrexian Germ creature token, then attach this to it.)\\nEquipped creature gets +0/+1 and has "Sacrifice this creature: This creature deals 1 damage to any target."\\nEquip {2}', 'Metalcraft — Ardent Recruit gets +2/+2 as long as you control three or more artifacts.', 'Metalcraft — This spell costs {1} less to cast if you control three or more artifacts.\\nCounter target spell.', 'Metalcraft — {T}: Tap target artifact, creature, or land. Activate only if you control three or more artifacts.', 'No more than one creature can attack each combat.\\nNo more than one creature can block each combat.', 'Other blue creatures you control get +1/+1.\\n{U}: Target artifact creature becomes blue until end of turn.\\nTap an untapped blue creature you control: Add {C}{C}. Spend this mana only to cast artifact spells or activate abilities of artifacts.', 'Prevent the next 3 damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn. For each 1 damage prevented this way, put a +1/+1 counter on that creature.', "Put X -1/-1 counters on each creature. Shuffle Black Sun's Zenith into its owner's library.", "Put target attacking creature on the bottom of its owner's library. Its controller gains life equal to its toughness.", 'Return up to two target creature cards from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Sacrifice Fume Spitter: Put a -1/-1 counter on target creature.', 'Sacrifice a creature: Add one mana of any color.', 'Sacrifice a creature: Phyrexian Ghoul gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Sacrifice a creature: Put a charge counter on Spawning Pit.\\n{1}, Remove two charge counters from Spawning Pit: Create a 2/2 colorless Spawn artifact creature token.', 'Sacrifice any number of artifacts, creatures, and/or lands. Draw a card for each permanent sacrificed this way.', 'Search your library for an Equipment card, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Tap target creature.\\nMetalcraft — If you control three or more artifacts, exile that creature.', 'Until end of turn, creatures you control get +1/+1 and gain trample and infect. (Creatures with infect deal damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters and to players in the form of poison counters.)', "Vigilance\\nWhen Glimmerpoint Stag enters the battlefield, exile another target permanent. Return that card to the battlefield under its owner's control at the beginning of the next end step.", 'When Contagion Clasp enters the battlefield, put a -1/-1 counter on target creature.\\n{4}, {T}: Proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', "When Diabolic Servitude enters the battlefield, return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nWhen the creature put onto the battlefield with Diabolic Servitude dies, exile it and return Diabolic Servitude to its owner's hand.\\nWhen Diabolic Servitude leaves the battlefield, exile the creature put onto the battlefield with Diabolic Servitude.", 'When Mitotic Slime dies, create two 2/2 green Ooze creature tokens. They have "When this creature dies, create two 1/1 green Ooze creature tokens."', 'When Myr Retriever dies, return another target artifact card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Myr Sire dies, create a 1/1 colorless Phyrexian Myr artifact creature token.', 'When Protean Hulk dies, search your library for any number of creature cards with total mana value 6 or less, put them onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'When Soul Snuffers enters the battlefield, put a -1/-1 counter on each creature.', 'When Symbiotic Elf dies, create two 1/1 green Insect creature tokens.', 'When Trinket Mage enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an artifact card with mana value 1 or less, reveal that card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'When Viridian Emissary dies, you may search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Wither (This deals damage to creatures in the form of -1/-1 counters.)\\nWhenever a creature an opponent controls with a -1/-1 counter on it dies, you may return that card to the battlefield under your control.', '{2}{B}{G}, Sacrifice a creature: Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Another target creature gets -2/-2 until end of turn.', '{T}, Sacrifice Phyrexian Plaguelord: Target creature gets -4/-4 until end of turn.\\nSacrifice a creature: Target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', '{T}, Sacrifice Terramorphic Expanse: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Proliferate. (Choose any number of permanents and/or players, then give each another counter of each kind already there.)', '{T}, Sacrifice three artifacts: Search your library for an artifact card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', "{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}: Blinkmoth Nexus becomes a 1/1 Blinkmoth artifact creature with flying until end of turn. It's still a land.\\n{1}, {T}: Target Blinkmoth creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Activate only if you control a Swamp.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Talisman of Progress deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {U}.', '{T}: Add {W}.']
flavor: ['"All matter, animate or not, rots when exposed to time. We merely speed up the process."\\n—Ezoc, Golgari rot farmer', '"An appropriately detailed model is indistinguishable from reality, and much easier to control."', '"Anything that watches without sleep and fights without fear is a valuable ally against the Phyrexians."\\n—Kara Vrist, Neurok agent', '"Death—an outmoded concept. We sleep, and we change."\\n—Sitrik, birth priest', '"In the game of conquest, who cares about the pawns if the king yet reigns?"\\n—Geth, keeper of the Vault', '"Let their mindless armies come and face the might of genius."\\n—Varil, Neurok partisan', '"Meat *and* eggs. We eat!"\\n—Borborygmos', '"Our archers made sport of it as it fumbled its way up the slag ridge. As it collapsed we thought ourselves safe, but the foul thing carried more than necrogen."\\n—Adaran, Tangle hunter', '"Phyrexians can\'t corrupt what they can\'t get close enough to touch."', '"The final stage of the illness: delirium, convulsions, and death."\\n—Phyrexian progress notes', '"Under the suns, Mirrodin kneels and begs us for perfection."\\n—Geth, Lord of the Vault', '"We lost our homes and our kin. We won\'t let those rotters take our future as well."', '"We sculpt the land into what we need—homes, armament, fortresses of war. Our strength comes not only from knowing, but from commanding the terrain."\\n—Raksha Golden Cub, leonin kha', '"Your life was meaningless, but your death will glorify Yawgmoth."\\n—Tsabo Tavoc', 'A beacon in the night, a dream in the fog.', 'A great mirage, a dream of wings and silver.', 'A mirror to draw its eye, a rod to rouse its rage, and a sword to break its bonds.', 'After the Battle of Liet Field, the white sun crested above Taj-Nar, bringing hope to all who survived the carnage.', 'Bladehold houses a rogues\' gallery filled with the living "statues" of the worst enemies of the Auriok.', 'Even the dead are raw materials for the Phyrexian vision of perfection.', 'Everything will find its use in Phyrexia. Eventually.', 'For the Phyrexians, death is not an end, nor a one-time occurrence.', 'For the first and last time, the horrific creature experienced terror.', 'Its precious corpses dance like puppets to attract mindless nim prey.', 'Life is ephemeral. Phyrexia is eternal.', 'Lumengrid, site of the Knowledge Pool, source of vedalken arcana.', 'Lymph, the fluid essence of blinkmoths, is prized by wizards for the rush of intellect it provides.', 'Mephidross gives up treasure easily... as long as you take its place.', 'Obsessed with the pursuit of knowledge above all else, vedalken can appear to be cold and emotionless.', 'Phyrexia wastes nothing. Its food chain is a spiraling cycle.', "Phyrexia's spiral of consumption grows ever wider and darker.", "Reminders of Memnarch's reign still skirr across Mirrodin, reminiscent of his form if not his power.", 'Scholars say that arbiters exist on every world, created by an unknown hand to enforce justice.', "She is the apex of the artificer's craft, the spirit of the divine called out of base metal.", 'Some blades seek their own wielders.', 'Taj-Nar, throne of Raksha Golden Cub, destined leader of the leonin prides.', 'The goblins say it used to be larger, before it began to stoke the Great Furnace with pieces of itself.', 'The myr are like quicksilver: malleable in function and adaptable in form.', 'The ultimate treasure is one that guards itself.', 'They once sought to unite with the flame of transcendence. Now they seek only to extinguish the lights of others.', 'They watch for a new master, one more sinister than the last.', 'Those who survive the test bear a mark of power anyone can recognize.', 'Venser wondered if it could still be called a teleportation spell if the destination is oblivion.', 'Where nature impedes, Phyrexians overcome.', 'Zombies mourn for the living and celebrate those who will soon be given the gift of death.']
artist: ['Alan Pollack', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Allen Williams', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Ben Thompson', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Brom', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chris Rahn', 'Daarken', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'David Day', 'Don Hazeltine', 'Efrem Palacios', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Erica Yang', 'Francis Tsai', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Izzy', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'Jason Felix', 'Jim Nelson', 'Johann Bodin', 'John Avon', 'Jung Park', 'Justin Sweet', 'Kaja Foglio', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kev Walker', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Marc Simonetti', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Mike Bierek', 'Mike Dringenberg', 'Nils Hamm', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pete Venters', 'Randis Albion', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rob Alexander', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Scott Chou', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Tony Szczudlo', 'Trevor Hairsine', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Wayne England', 'Whit Brachna', 'jD']
